---
import "../styles/global.css";
import GoogleAnalytics from "../components/GoogleAnalytics.astro";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How Hacks² reviews tools, handles recommendations and may earn from affiliate partnerships."
    />
    <meta name="robots" content="index,follow" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://hacks2.com/disclosure/" />
    <title>Editorial & Affiliate Disclosure — Hacks²</title>
    <GoogleAnalytics />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page-shell">
      <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Hacks squared home">
          <span class="mark">H²</span>
          <span>Hacks² / Applied AI</span>
        </a>
        <div class="nav-links">
          <a href="/workflows/">Workflows</a>
          <a href="/tools/">Tools</a>
          <a href="/notes/">Field Notes</a>
          <a class="nav-product-link" href="/business-operations-pack/">Operations Pack</a>
        </div>
        <span class="nav-menu">Policy / 001</span>
      </nav>

      <article class="article-shell">
        <header class="article-header">
          <span class="section-tag">Transparency</span>
          <h1>Editorial &<br />affiliate disclosure.</h1>
          <p>Hacks² exists to help people choose and apply AI tools with better judgment.</p>
        </header>

        <aside class="article-rail">
          <div>
            <span>Principle</span>
            <p>Recommendations must remain useful even when no commercial relationship exists.</p>
          </div>
        </aside>

        <div class="article-content">
          <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
          <p>Tool reviews, workflows and field notes are selected because they may help readers do better work. A commercial relationship never guarantees coverage or a positive recommendation.</p>

          <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
          <p>Some external links may later become affiliate links. If a reader signs up or buys through one of them, Hacks² may receive a commission at no additional cost to the reader.</p>
          <p>When this applies, the relevant page will state it clearly near the recommendation. We will not disguise promotional links as independent advice.</p>

          <h2>How tools are assessed</h2>
          <p>We look for a clear use case, practical value, limitations, pricing context and whether the tool improves a real workflow. A large feature list is not enough.</p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>For corrections, partnership enquiries or disclosure questions, use the contact details that will be published on Hacks².</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <section class="article-next">
        <span class="section-tag">Explore the index</span>
        <a href="/tools/">See the recommended tools <span>↗</span></a>
      </section>

      <footer class="footer">
        <span>© 2026 Hacks²</span>
        <span>Built for applied intelligence</span>
        <a href="/disclosure/">Editorial disclosure</a>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
